/*!
	\mainpage NewGUI API Reference

	NewGUI is a cross-platform UI toolkit in C++23 whose architecture follows
	the Interface Kit of Haiku: one looper per window, messages, a persistent
	view tree, constraint layout and exchangeable looks.

	The project is in its early port phase; there is no stable API yet. The
	specification, the conventions and the test evidence are on the
	<a href="../">documentation site</a>.
*/


/*!
	\namespace ngui
	\brief All of NewGUI. Submodules are nested namespaces (ngui::gfx ...).
*/


/*!
	\namespace ngui::gfx
	\brief Geometry and color types of the Canvas layer (specification 4 and 5).
*/


/*!
	\namespace ngui::test
	\brief The test kit (specification 20 and 21): offscreen rendering, image
	comparison with the tolerances of 21.2, and snapshots with their reports.
	Library ngui_testkit; GoogleTest macros in ngui/test/GTest.h.
*/


/*!
	\namespace ngui::platform
	\brief The platform layer (modules P1, P2): windows, screens and the events
	of the window system, and the CPU presenter that shows rendered pixels.
*/


/*!
	\namespace ngui::platform::sdl3
	\brief Internals of the SDL3 platform (SdlPlatform).
*/


/*!
	\namespace ngui::text
	\brief The text subsystem (modules X1, X2, X5): fonts, shaping with
	HarfBuzz, metrics and truncation. Library ngui_text with the bundled Noto
	fonts (vcpkg feature text, NGUI_WITH_TEXT).
*/

